// The inline content of a Markdown file, its file's programs (decisions 0238, 0431 §4). tree-sitter-md reads a
// Markdown file in two grammars: the block grammar gives the file's tree (headings, lists, paragraphs, code blocks),
// and each `inline` and `pipe_table_cell` node of it holds text in the inline grammar (`markdown-inline`: emphasis,
// links, code spans, inline HTML). Each such node holds a program of that grammar.
//
//   > Some *text* and a [link](u)       block: block_quote > paragraph > inline
//   > on two lines.                     inline program: emphasis, inline_link > link_text, link_destination
//
// A program's text is the node's without the block continuations inside it (the `> ` above), and its nodes have the
// file's lines and columns. The Markdown language declares the programs (`languages/markdown.json`'s `embeds`, built
// by `embed::inline_content` from the file's tape at its load), so this library derives nothing: a rule reaches one
// through `parsed(i, "markdown-inline", r)` at its `inline` i.
